我觉得它很有意思。

297
00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.320
And it's an alt.
而且那是一个备选方案。

298
00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:32.420
They ultimately end up providing this information with Dwight later.
他们最终还是在后面通过德怀特提供了这些信息。

299
00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.960
But there was a scene with Michael by himself.
但原本有一个迈克尔独自一人的场景。

300
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.200
And it's the start of his day.
那是他一天的开始。

301
00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.160
And he's driving into work.
他正开车去上班。

302
00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:44.340
He's doing one of those driving talking heads that Michael does, right?
他正在拍那种迈克尔常拍的开车访谈，对吧？

303
00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:47.440
Oh, well, the last time he did that, it was very dangerous.
噢，上次他那样做的时候，真的很危险。

304
00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.100
I know.
我知道。

305
00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.540
He hit an employee.
他撞到了一名员工。

306
00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.020
He did.
确实撞了。

307
00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.180
So it's the same thing.
所以这次也是一样。

308
00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.120
He's driving into work.
他正开车去上班。

309
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.400
And he's sort of showing off his rental car.
而且他还在炫耀他的租用车。

310
00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.040
It looks like a Ford Taurus.
看起来像是辆福特金牛座。

311
00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.280
Yes, I see Ford.
没错，我看到了福特的标志。

312
00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.000
I think Taurus.
我觉得是金牛座。

313
00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:58.760
I don't know, guys.
我不太确定，伙计们。

314
00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.160
Correct me if I'm wrong on that.
如果我说错了请纠正我。

315
00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:05.480
But we learn the whole backstory, why he's not driving the Sebring.
但我们了解了整个背景故事，为什么他没开那辆赛百灵。

316
00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:11.220
Michael said he had to get a rental car because his Sebring is in the body shop because Meredith
迈克尔说他不得不租车，因为他的赛百灵在修理厂，那是梅雷迪斯

317
00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.760
left a big dent in the hood.
在引擎盖上撞了个大坑。

318
00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.540
And then he said, but listen, this rental has navigation.
然后他说，但听着，这辆租用车有导航系统。

319
00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:23.640
And Michael calls it his invisible driving companion.
迈克尔管它叫他的隐形驾驶伴侣。

320
00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.160
And he goes, but, you know, listen, it is really amazing.
他说，但你知道，听着，这真的很神奇。

321
00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.880
And it's like a computerized map in your car.
就像车里装了个电脑地图一样。

322
00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:36.680
And he goes on to say that he loves its voice, that he finds it so soothing.
接着他说他很喜欢那个声音，觉得非常悦耳。

323
00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.120
It's like taking a warm bath.
就像洗了个热水澡一样舒服。

324
00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:45.080
And while he's saying how much he loves the voice, Jan calls.
就在他夸赞那个声音有多好听的时候，简打来了电话。

325
00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.740
And this is what we hear.
然后我们听到了这些。

326
00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.080
Sam, will you play that?
萨姆，能放一下那段吗？

327
00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.870
Oh, hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on.
噢，等等，等等，等等，等等。

328
00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:56.890
Ah, it is my lady love.
啊，是我的爱人。

329
00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:57.890
Smilow.
斯迈洛。

330
00:15:58.170 --> 00:15:59.970
Where the f*** are my grape nuts?
我的葡萄干麦片到底去哪儿了？

331
00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:00.890
I don't.
我不知道。

332
00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.970
I just want to know, did you eat my grape nuts?
我只想知道，是不是你吃了我的葡萄干麦片？

333
00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.910
Ah, no, I hate those things.
啊，没有，我讨厌那玩意儿。

334
00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:05.750
Grow up, Michael.
成熟点吧，迈克尔。

335
00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:10.340
I love, not a morning person.
我喜欢，不是个早起的人。

336
00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:19.580
After that, he sits in the car in silence and he just hits the navigation button.
在那之后，他坐在车里沉默不语，只是按下了导航按钮。

337
00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.160
So it just keeps talking to him.
于是它就一直对他说话。

338
00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:22.380
You have arrived.
您已到达目的地。

339
00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:26.060
You have, it's like, it just, he just needs something soothing.
你瞧，就像是，他只是需要一些抚慰。

340
00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:27.040
Oh, lady.
噢，女士。

341
00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:29.300
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

342
00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:30.780
Wow.
哇。

343
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:34.320
Just a window into his life with Jan.
这简直是他和简生活的一扇窗口。

344
00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.840
And maybe a little bit of the reason why he trusts the navigation so much.
也许这就是他为什么那么信任导航的原因。

345
00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.560
Because it's just this soothing, invisible driving companion.
因为它只是一个抚慰人心的隐形驾驶伴侣。

346
00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.400
Yeah, I get that.
是啊，我明白。

347
00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:49.840
So, yes, this episode actually does start with the conference room.
所以，没错，这一集确实是从会议室开始的。

348
00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:52.900
Jenna, did you see the spread on that table?
珍娜，你看到桌上摆的那些食物了吗？

349
00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:54.560
It was incredible.
简直太棒了。

350
00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.460
I remember it from shooting.
我还记得拍摄时的情况。

351
00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.840
They had excellent, excellent little snacks and treats.
他们准备了非常、非常棒的小零食和点心。

352
00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:01.460
Excellent.
太棒了。

353
00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:06.960
In fact, Michael says that he got the finest gourmet items that Scranton has to offer.
事实上，迈克尔说他弄到了斯克兰顿能提供的最好的美食。

354
00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.440
How much did this all cost?
这一切花了多少钱？

355
00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:17.880
I love every time you ask that question, you are personally fascinated by how Michael funds
我喜欢你每次问这个问题，你对迈克尔如何资助

356
00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:20.040
all of his extracurriculars.
他所有的课外活动感到非常好奇。

357
00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.200
And it's such a good question to ask.
而且这是一个非常好的问题。

358
00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:27.580
It's, this is where Angela Martin, the accountant character, bleeds into your real personality.
这就是安吉拉·马丁这个会计角色与你真实性格重合的地方。

359
00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:30.820
It is, because let me tell you, those baskets were not cheap.
确实，因为我告诉你，那些篮子可不便宜。

360
00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:31.460
Look at those.
看看那些篮子。

361
00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:32.680
I love baskets.
我喜欢篮子。

362
00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.000
My husband says my nickname should be baskets.
我丈夫说我的绰号应该叫“篮子”。

363
00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.940
I have a basket problem.
我有篮子成瘾的问题。

364
00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:39.780
If I see a basket, I'm going to buy it.
只要我看到篮子，我就一定会买。

365
00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:43.820
And I'm telling you, those baskets are primo baskets.
我跟你说，那些篮子可是顶级货。

366
00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:49.780
Angela, I know that you recently did a huge clean out of your garage.
安吉拉，我知道你最近清理了你的车库。

367
00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.640
I did.
是的，我清理了。

368
00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:55.760
Will you share with us how many baskets were in the garage?
你能和我们分享一下车库里有多少个篮子吗？

369
00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:57.740
37.
37个。

370
00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.600
Yeah, 37.
没错，37个。

371
00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:02.940
How many did you keep?
你留下了多少个？

372
00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:04.740
12.
12个。

373
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.280
I picked my 12 favorite.
我挑出了我最喜欢的12个。

374
00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.080
And let me tell you, it was hard for me to let go.
我得说，要我放手真的很难。

375
00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.380
I donated them to a church in our neighborhood that does outreach.
我把它们捐给了我们附近的一个教会，他们会做慈善外展活动。

376
00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:18.780
And I was very, very happy that they got my baskets, but it was hard to say goodbye.
我非常、非常高兴他们收到了我的篮子，但要告别它们真的很难。

377
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:25.980
I felt like when you were leaving me messages about this, I was really proud of you for this
当你给我留言说这件事的时候，我真的为你取得的进步感到骄傲。

378
00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:26.660
progress.
进步。

379
00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.280
Thank you.
谢谢。

380
00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.740
With your basket issue.
关于你的篮子问题。

381
00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:30.400
Thank you.
谢谢。

382
00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:31.920
Yeah.
是啊。

383
00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.860
That's not counting how many baskets I have inside the house.
这还没算上我屋子里有多少个篮子呢。

384
00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.200
Oh, no.
哦，不。

385
00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.640
That I'm using, though.
不过那些我都在用。

386
00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.620
Like, I have a basket, Jenna, by the fireplace that I roll up and I put blankets in.
比如，珍娜，我在壁炉旁放了一个篮子，用来卷放毯子。

387
00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:46.860
And then I have a basket in my bedroom that I roll up and put blankets in.
然后我在卧室里也放了一个篮子，用来卷放毯子。

388
00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:50.460
Listen, I have a lot of blankets around my house because my husband is a giant mountain man,
听着，我家里有很多毯子，因为我丈夫是个像山一样高大的男人，

389
00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.660
and I'm always freezing.
而我总是觉得冷。

390
00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:53.400
He runs hot.
他总是觉得热。

391
00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:57.280
But I have baskets of blankets stashed all around.
所以我到处都藏着装满毯子的篮子。

392
00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:58.020
Okay.
好吧。

393
00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:03.520
That is the title of your autobiography, Baskets of Blankets by Angela Kinsey.
这就是你自传的标题了，《毯子篮》，作者安吉拉·金赛。

394
00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.120
With a side of donuts and a glass of wine.
再配上一份甜甜圈和一杯红酒。

395
00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:07.900
It's a very long title.
这书名太长了。

396
00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.090
One million copies already sold.
已经卖出一百万册了。

397
00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:12.370
Yep.
没错。

398
00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:14.310
All right.
好吧。

399
00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:19.930
Well, Michael has this talking head where he explains what these baskets are all about.
迈克尔有个采访片段，他在里面解释了这些篮子的用意。

400
00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:25.430
He says, you know, Ryan thinks everything is about emails and I aMs.
他说，瑞安觉得一切都靠电子邮件和即时通讯，而我……

401
00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:26.690
It's all about technology.
一切都与科技有关。

402
00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:34.710
But he's forgetting about the original instant message, which is a letter attached to a basket of food.
但他忘了最初的即时通讯方式，其实是把信绑在装食物的篮子上。

403
00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:34.970
Yeah.
没错。

404
00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.270
That's the original I am, you guys.
那才是最初的即时通讯，各位。

405
00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:39.490
In case you were wondering.
以防你们好奇的话。

406
00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:50.370
Well, I guess speaking of the cost of these baskets, Dwight is going to turn in receipts for the cost of these gift baskets to Angela.
说到这些篮子的成本，德怀特打算把这些礼品篮的收据交给安吉拉报销。

407
00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:50.810
Yeah.
是啊。

408
00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:54.190
Who is very, very icy toward him.
而安吉拉对他非常非常冷淡。

409
00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:54.770
Yeah.
没错。

410
00:19:55.050 --> 00:20:02.570
And before we get into the scene, Jenna, we've brought this up before, but for any of you that missed it, 22 minutes, 53 seconds,
在进入正题之前，珍娜，我们之前提过，但如果有人错过了，在22分53秒处，

411
00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:11.570
you can clearly see on the message board under thus, T-H-U-S, thus, the following caption.
你可以清楚地看到留言板上在“thus”（因此）这个词下方，有这样一段说明。

412
00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.850
In case you haven't noticed, there's a lot of colorful Huey on this board.
如果你还没注意到的话，这块板子上有很多彩色的休伊。

413
00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:24.950
Well, it's interesting you mentioned that, Angela, because we had several people write in about this whiteboard behind you.
安吉拉，你提到这个很有意思，因为有几个人写信问起你身后的这块白板。

414
00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:31.970
Katie E., Julie Bird, and Christopher Neville all said that there's even more stuff on the board now.
凯蒂·E、朱莉·伯德和克里斯托弗·内维尔都说现在板子上的内容更多了。

415
00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:38.410
For example, there is an Anger Management Appreciation Day on Tuesday, the 23rd.
比如，23号星期二有“愤怒管理感谢日”。

416
00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:46.490
On the 8th, there is an Accounting Department meeting, and it specifies, be prepared to show your work.
8号有会计部会议，上面特别注明：准备好展示你的工作成果。

417
00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:56.070
And on the 10th, it says flex times, which, interestingly enough, includes Karen, even though she left.
10号写着弹性工作时间，有趣的是，这还包括凯伦，尽管她已经离职了。

418
00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:03.750
And under the flex times on the 10th, it says that Ryan will cover reception, even though he now works at corporate.
在10号的弹性工作时间下方，写着瑞安将负责前台接待，尽管他现在在总公司工作。

419
00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:05.630
Yeah.
是啊。

420
00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.590
And what is a flex time?
那什么是弹性工作时间呢？

421
00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:17.390
You know, when I worked in admin, you needed to give the front receptionist a break so that that person could go to lunch.
你知道，我以前在行政部门工作时，需要给前台接待员休息时间，好让她去吃午饭。

422
00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:17.610
Yeah.
没错。

423
00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:23.490
And so the other admin desks would rotate in to sit at the desk for lunch.
所以其他行政人员会轮流去前台值班，顶替她的午休时间。

424
00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:26.950
So I was usually the receptionist,
我通常是那个接待员，

425
00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:34.570
and then each day a different admin would take over my lunch hour because you couldn't have no one answering front reception or no one greeting guests.
每天会有不同的行政人员接替我的午餐时间，因为不能没人接听前台电话或接待访客。

426
00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:42.050
So I always assumed that's what it meant, that flex time was who rotated to give Pam her lunch break.
所以我一直以为这就是它的意思，弹性工作时间就是指谁来轮班顶替帕姆的午休。

427
00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:43.970
But I don't know.
但我也不确定。

428
00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:45.670
I would have loved to have seen that scene.
我真希望能看到那一幕。

429
00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:50.990
I would have loved to have seen, like, just a montage of, like, different people answering the phones.
我真希望能看到一段剪辑，展示不同的人接听电话的样子。

430
00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:54.830
Well, yes.
嗯，确实。

431
00:21:55.050 --> 00:22:01.390
So Dwight hands Angela the receipt for all the items in the baskets, and she's very icy towards him, Jenna.
德怀特把篮子里所有物品的收据交给安吉拉，她对他非常冷淡，珍娜。

432
00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:05.210
She just wants it to be business, just business.
她只想公事公办，纯粹的公事。

433
00:22:05.770 --> 00:22:06.190
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:07.510
And he says, I miss you.
然后他说，我好想你。

435
00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:09.090
And she's like, elevators.
她说，电梯。

436
00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:09.870
Yeah.
没错。

437
00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:14.630
And then when they get to the elevators, Angela's making it very clear that it's over.
当他们走到电梯时，安吉拉明确表示一切都结束了。

438
00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:17.210
And Dwight is kind of like, okay, okay.
德怀特表现得像是，好吧，好吧。

439
00:22:17.870 --> 00:22:19.690
I do want to be friends.
我确实想和你做朋友。

440
00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:22.950
Plus a little extra, also, I love you.
外加一点点额外的东西，还有，我爱你。

441
00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:26.810
This is one of my favorite things that Dwight ever says to Angela.
这是德怀特对安吉拉说过的话里，我最喜欢的一句。

442
00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:30.070
I have seen this, like, stitched on a pillow.
我甚至见过有人把它绣在枕头上。

443
00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:32.990
I've seen it on all of these Valentine's iteMs.
我在各种情人节礼品上都见过。

444
00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:34.130
It's really cute.
真的很可爱。

445
00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:40.430
People have written this to their boyfriend or girlfriend, and they've shared it with me online.
人们把它写给自己的男朋友或女朋友，还在网上分享给我看。

446
00:22:40.430 --> 00:22:43.550
But that, plus a little extra, also, I love you.
